				1739,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Correct stub format for ExtensionsManifest in build script\n\nUpdate the `build.rs` script to write a valid `CacheBlob` JSON structure instead of a bare JSON array when generating the stub `extensions.manifest.json`. The `LoadFromCache` parser expects an object containing `version`, `count`, and `extensions` fields, whereas the previous implementation wrote `[]`, causing potential parsing mismatches or type errors during startup.\n\nThis ensures the Tauri build process generates a structurally correct manifest stub that aligns with the runtime data deserialization expectations, preventing crashes when the Sky-generated manifest is unavailable.",
			"SHA": "8924f19f5908567bc989f640cbf8626ba937dacf"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T06:28:37Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1739,
				4
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Standardize DTO naming and repair UTF-8 path handling\n\nAlign `ModelVersionIdentifier` to `ModelVersionId` in `MarkerDataDTO` and `DiagnosticProvider` to match existing PascalCase conventions and reduce verbosity.\n\nEnhance the `FileWriteNative` IPC handler to detect and decode base64-encoded buffers received from VS Code serialization paths, falling back to raw bytes if decoding fails. This resolves data corruption when saving files via certain extension workflows.\n\nRewrite `percent_decode` in `PathExtraction` to correctly reconstruct multi-byte UTF-8 sequences from percent-encoded URI components. The previous implementation cast decoded bytes directly to `char`, corrupting non-ASCII paths (e.g., CJK or accented characters) and causing silent ENOENT errors. The new approach accumulates raw bytes and performs a safe `from_utf8` conversion with a lossy fallback.\n\nThese changes ensure robust file operations with international paths and consistent data integrity across the IPC layer.",
			"SHA": "1ee9d6c0f0082ba72857e78be4316b0abb8af829"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T06:03:46Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1739,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Preserve binary integrity in HTTP response parsing\n\nThe `forward_http_request` helper in `Source/Binary/Build/Scheme.rs` was incorrectly converting HTTP response bodies to UTF-8 strings before parsing. This `String::from_utf8_lossy` operation corrupted binary content (images, WASM modules, etc.) by inserting replacement characters for non-UTF-8 sequences.\n\nUpdate `parse_http_response` to accept a raw byte slice (`&[u8]`) instead of a `&str`. Implement the header/body separation using `windows(4)` to locate the `\\r\\n\\r\\n` separator on raw bytes. Safely decode only the header section to UTF-8 (since HTTP headers are ASCII), while passing the body bytes directly to the result tuple.\n\nThis ensures binary assets proxied through the Mountain build tool remain intact and prevents data corruption during HTTP forwarding.",
			"SHA": "977f678a3ae277ac8d8f21db1cbe3be48690a369"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T05:34:02Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1739,
				4
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Extend extension cache lifetime and refine SCM updates\n\nIncrease the maximum cache age for extension descriptors from 10 minutes to 24 hours. The previous window was too tight for local development workflows where the binary and cache are co-located; since builds regenerate the cache, a longer duration prevents unnecessary rescans without staleness risks.\n\nEnhance the `FileWriteNative` handler to suppress false-positive warnings when the Cocoon process is not yet connected during `FileWrite` operations. This prevents noise in the `vfs` log when saving files before the extension host is fully ready.\n\nAlign `UpdateScmGroup` logic to emit `scmId` alongside `providerId` in the payload to `sky://scm/updateGroup`. This ensures the Sky frontend can correctly resolve the SCM shim. Remove the fallback logic that attempted to invoke `UpdateSourceControlGroup` traits, as direct event emission is the reliable path.\n\nAdditionally, add `DebugServer`, `DebugServerPortMountain`, and `DebugServerPortCocoon` to the environment variable whitelist in `CocoonManagement` to support future debugging configurations.",
			"SHA": "fc1e6daf52356219f8c954cc53b698a688432d94"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T05:33:57Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1739,
				2
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Prevent Tauri build failure on missing Sky manifest\n\nThe Tauri build process fails when running `cargo build` directly because it validates `extensions.manifest.json` referenced in `bundle.resources`, which is normally generated by the Sky frontend build. Update `build.rs` to create a stub file (`[]`) at the expected path if missing, ensuring the build succeeds without a prior Sky build while retaining the live scan fallback in `LoadFromCache.rs`.\n\nAdditionally, disable `beforeBundleCommand` in `tauri.conf.json` to prevent redundant or conflicting manifest generation steps during the Tauri build phase, relying instead on the explicit manifest creation in `build.rs` and the existing Sky build pipeline.",
			"SHA": "3473a81e819f0b8a80fc02084589693a1fe0d85d"
		}
	],
